step_by_step:
Analysis: Article 51 of the Indian Constitution, under Part IV (Directive Principles of State Policy), mandates that the State shall endeavour to:
(a) Promote international peace and security;
(b) Maintain just and honourable relations between nations;
(c) Foster respect for international law and treaty obligations;
(d) Encourage settlement of international disputes by arbitration.

solution.detailed:
Article 51 of the Indian Constitution, under Part IV (Directive Principles of State Policy), mandates that the State shall endeavour to:
(a) Promote international peace and security;
(b) Maintain just and honourable relations between nations;
(c) Foster respect for international law and treaty obligations;
(d) Encourage settlement of international disputes by arbitration.
